coder › Implemented `parseMoney` in `src/money.ts` and added tests in `src/money.test.ts`.

What changed
- `parseMoney(text)` now:
  - Detects the currency from `€/EUR`, `$/USD`, `£/GBP` anywhere in the text and returns `{ cents, currency }`.
  - Throws `TypeError` (message includes the offending text) when there is no recognized currency, when more than one distinct currency is named, or when there are no digits.
  - Strips the currency token(s), then reads the amount.
  - Treats the last comma/dot as a decimal separator only when it is followed by exactly two digits at the end; every other comma/dot and all spaces are grouping.
  - Handles a leading `-` and parentheses around the amount as negative.
  - Normalizes a negative zero amount to `0` cents.

Decisions beyond the plan
- Conflicting currencies (e.g. `€100 USD`) throw a `TypeError` — the spec only defines reading one currency, so I treated multiple distinct ones as invalid.
- Negative zero (`-€0,00`) returns `0` rather than `-0`.

